# Build output. Covers everything Gradle generates in both projects: generated-src (the ANTLR
# parser), classes, test-results, reports, the jacoco *.exec files and the assembled jars.
build/
cli/build/
.gradle/

# Maven is gone (pom.xml was deleted with the Gradle migration), but this stays ignored: IDE Java
# language servers that imported this project as a Maven module keep compiling into target/classes
# and target/test-classes from their own cached config, which lives outside the repo and does not
# notice that pom.xml disappeared. Re-importing the project as Gradle stops it; until every
# developer has done that, an unignored target/ dumps ~140 untracked files into `git status`.
target/


# The wrapper script and JAR ARE committed, deliberately: `./gradlew` must work in a fresh
# checkout. That is what lets the Makefile be the only entry point and CI use the same Gradle
# version a developer does.

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything under src/test/resources/ IS committed, deliberately: CI checks out only this
# repository, and a fixture it cannot see would make every parity assertion skip silently.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT ignore src/test/resources/reference_parses/*.json
#
# Those 46 files look like temp output because of their hash-suffixed names
# (QUERY_scaninfo_MS1DATA__WHERE_MS1MZ_425.2898TOLERA___106d511f8de4ae41364fbece4838e2c8.json)
# but that is MassQL's own test-corpus naming and they are REQUIRED fixtures.
# ParseConformanceTest reads every one and asserts the count is exactly 46, so ignoring them
# turns the parser conformance suite into a vacuous pass and then a hard failure.
#
# Same for reference_parses/corpus-manifest.tsv: it is a checked-in record of the expected
# parser disposition, not generated noise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
